Landing end, per screen at runtime:
- RegionJourneyAdapter sets L.landing=lakesideRouteLanding(L) at journey prepare:
  LakesideCameraLayout.lakesideScreenLanding(journey, lakesideScreenFrame(viewport, boardSafeInsets)),
  i.e. the board UI's own frame.
- The arrival aim (new RegionJourneyCore key arrivalYawDeg, plus arrivalPitchDeg) and arrivalFovDeg are
  replaced by that screen's board camera (lakesideAlignedLookAt). The lens position is unchanged.
- The screen difference rides on the arrival smootherstep (last 14.3 m, >= 6 s of walk) with one weight
  for view and FOV, so the zoom is monotonic and nothing is left for the hook.
- The base landing numbers (close fallback-like pose; aim and FOV near a common phone's board camera)
  are used only if the screen cannot be read.
- Portrait board camera: position = the landing position; yaw and pitch solved so the 3D board centre
  sits on the 2D grid centre; FOV solved so the centre row matches the 2D grid width. Landscape unchanged.
- arrivalFovDeg (FOV eases with the arrival weight) and the C2 softClamp/timing work are carried over
  from the lakeside camera rounds. Not used elsewhere: arrivalYawToHer (dropped).

Hook (region/LakesideLandingHook.ts, lakesideLandingToBoard):
- Waits for prewarmLakesideAssets, at most 3 s counted in frames. If it fails or times out, the hook
  returns {ok:false,'lakeside-assets-not-ready'} with no camera write, and enterSelectedLevel runs the
  existing lakesideFallback('board'): [QF_LAKE] goes to the log only, back to the island, and the HUD
  shows the toast. Never an empty board.
- Otherwise it blends (position lerp + slerp + FOV, one smootherstep, 1 s) from the journey end to the
  board camera of the same frame and ends exactly on it; the lease camera takes over at that pose.
- With the journey solved for the same screen, the residual is ~0. It is non-zero only after a
  viewport change; beyond 10 deg view / 15 deg FOV, or off the landing position, it does a plain cut.
- Never rejects; with no deps it resolves {ok:true} at once.
- ui/BoardLayout.boardSafeInsets = ManagedMobileBoardUI.safeInsets moved verbatim (no behaviour
  change; the UI calls it).

Tests:
- test-lakeside-landing-hook (new): five screens (390x844, 414x896, 360x780, 375x667, 390x520). Per
  screen: journey end = board camera, hook residual <= 2 deg view / 3 deg FOV, the arrival window,
  her framing, per-frame data for the last 3 s and the hook.
- Failure path (rejected or hung preload), viewport change, never-rejects.
- test-lakeside-camera: K4/K5/K8 run per screen landing.
- test-lakeside-journey-wire: the call site and the fallback.
